Thanks for the report.

I agree with Ivan that `pd->numDefns` should be accurate at the first allocation, i.e., ...

```
Index: src/library/grDevices/src/devPS.c
===================================================================
--- src/library/grDevices/src/devPS.c	(revision 90939)
+++ src/library/grDevices/src/devPS.c	(working copy)
@@ -7920,8 +7920,9 @@
     nmask = pd->numMasks;
     npattern = countPatterns(pd);

-    if(pd->nobjs + nraster + nmask + npattern + 500 >= pd->max_nobjs) {
-	int new =  pd->nobjs + nraster + nmask + npattern + 500;
+    if(pd->nobjs + nraster + nmask + npattern + pd->numDefns + 500 >= 
+       pd->max_nobjs) {
+	int new =  pd->nobjs + nraster + nmask + npattern + pd->numDefns + 500;
 	void *tmp = realloc(pd->pos, new * sizeof(int));
 	if(!tmp)
 	    error("unable to increase object limit: please shutdown the pdf device");
```

I think keeping `npattern` is a double-count, but that should not be harmful (and is a lot less harmful than the current under-count).

That passes your example (and `make check-all`) for me.

Could you confirm this fixes things for you?
